Factur-X / ZUGFeRD
==================

The artifact redistributes, unmodified, the technical artifacts (schemas
and Schematron) of the Factur-X / ZUGFeRD standard published by FeRD
(Forum elektronische Rechnung Deutschland, AWV e.V.) and FNFE-MPE:

  ZUGFeRD 2.5.2 / Factur-X 1.09.2, release 2026-08-04
  https://www.ferd-net.de/publikationen-produkte/publikationen/detailseite/zugferd-252-deutsch
  File: io/github/nalukit/paniolo/rules/facturx/<archive>.zip
  (exact version and SHA-256 in facturx-rules.properties next to it)

The archive contains, for the profiles MINIMUM, BASIC WL, BASIC, EN 16931
and EXTENDED, the XSD schemas, the Schematron, the compiled Schematron XSLT
and the code lists of the folder "Schema" of the release package, with
their original names and folders. SHA256SUMS in the archive lists the
checksum of each file as published.

  Apache License, Version 2.0 (META-INF/licenses/Apache-2.0.txt)
  "Fuer die Nutzung der Technischen Artefakte (Schemata und Schematron) des
  ZUGFeRD-Standards gelten die Apache 2.0 Lizenzbedingungen."
  https://www.ferd-net.de/ueber-uns/ressourcen-1/veroeffentlichungen/haftungsausschluss-und-nutzungsrechte

ZUGFeRD 2.5.2 (c) 2026 FNFE-MPE | FeRD. Factur-X and ZUGFeRD are an
application of EN 16931-1 and CEN/TS 16931-3-3; the content of these
publications is used with the permission of CEN and DIN, which hold their
copyright. The Factur-X / ZUGFeRD schemas are based on the UN/CEFACT Cross
Industry Invoice (CII, D22B) and the UN/CEFACT Supply Chain Reference Data
Model; the code lists refer to UN/CEFACT and UNECE code lists (UNTDID,
UN/ECE Recommendations 20 and 21). Copyright of these works: UN/CEFACT and
UNECE; their terms of use apply accordingly.

ZUGFeRD 1.0
-----------

The archive io/github/nalukit/paniolo/rules/facturx/zugferd-1.0-2014-06-25.zip
holds the XSD schemas and the Schematron of ZUGFeRD 1.0 (FeRD, 2014-06-25),
which FeRD no longer publishes. They are taken unmodified from the Mustang
project (https://github.com/ZUGFeRD/mustangproject, Apache License 2.0),
as last changed there in commit 42795b17 (2021-05-09):

  schema/ZUGFeRD1p0*.xsd          validator/src/main/resources/schema/ZF_10/
  schematron/ZUGFeRD_1p0.sch      validator/src/main/resources/ZUGFeRD_1p0.sch
  schematron/ZUGFeRD_1p0.xslt     validator/src/main/resources/xslt/ZUGFeRD_1p0.xslt
                                  (the Schematron compiled to XSLT by the
                                  Mustang project)

SHA256SUMS in the archive lists the checksum of each file. The Schematron
carries the original terms of use of FeRD for the ZUGFeRD data format 1.0
(free licence for the use and further development of the data format in
software); FeRD states that the Apache License 2.0 applies to the technical
artifacts (schemas and Schematron) of the ZUGFeRD standard (see above).
Mustangproject, Copyright 2014 Jochen Staerk, Apache License 2.0.

