Order-X 1.0
-----------

The archive io/github/nalukit/paniolo/rules/facturx/order-x-1.0-2021-04-13.zip
holds the technical artifacts of Order-X 1.0 (English release of
2021-04-13), published by AWV e.V. (FeRD) and FNFE-MPE: for the profiles
Basic, Comfort and Extended the XSD schemas and the Schematron of the
folder 04-XSD-UML-SCHEMATRON, unmodified and with their original paths,
and the terms of use of the release (Nutzungsrechte.txt, Disclaimer.txt):

  "The Apache 2.0 license terms apply to the use of the Order-X technical
  artifacts."

The files <level>/Schematron/SCRDMCCBDACIOMessageStructure_100pD20B_<LEVEL>.xslt
are not part of the release: they are the Schematron of the release
compiled to XSLT with SVRL output by Paniolo (scripts/package-orderx-rules.sh,
ISO Schematron skeleton, MIT License, and Saxon-HE). SHA256SUMS in the
archive marks each file as official or compiled. Order-X is based on the
UN/CEFACT Supply Chain Reference Data Model and the Cross Industry Order;
the terms of use of UNECE apply accordingly.

The generated XSLT files include utility templates from the ISO Schematron
skeleton by Rick Jelliffe and Academia Sinica Computing Centre, Taiwan:
  https://github.com/Schematron/schematron/tree/master/trunk/schematron/code
Their MIT license and copyright notices are retained in
META-INF/licenses/MIT-ISO-Schematron.txt and in
licenses/MIT-ISO-Schematron.txt inside the Order-X archive.
